            "subject": "Stop claiming a restore succeeded when the server says otherwise",
            "body": "Stop claiming a restore succeeded when the server says otherwise\n\nrestorePremium() reports RevenueCat's view, and after Apple moves a subscription\nto another account RevenueCat still reports an active entitlement — while the\nserver has granted nothing. The OR meant the user saw \"Compras restauradas\", was\nsent to the dashboard, and remained locked out.\n\nThe server is the source of truth everywhere else in this design; this line was\nthe one place that forgot. An honest \"no purchases found\" sends them to support\ninstead of leaving them to wonder whether they were charged.\n\nSeen for real: a sandbox purchase transferred from user 1 to user 69, RevenueCat\nactive, server not.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015XAnzXatq9LE84zyNc4yw9\n",
            "author": {
